# The `+` and `.` between product patterns, in the shapes a check made bond
# by bond cannot decide (issue #104, and the shapes found with it).
#
# BioNetGen applies all of a rule's operations, then splits the result into
# connected components (SpeciesGraph::splitConnectedComponents) and checks
# them (RxnRule::apply_rule).  A component holding molecules the rule maps
# into two product patterns breaks a `+`.  A product pattern whose molecules
# lie in two components breaks a `.`.  A component holding none of the
# molecules the rule names is a species the rule does not write, which only
# DeleteMolecules allows.  RuleMonkey tested the `+` and `.` at the two ends
# of each deleted bond.  That cannot decide a molecule deleted out of a
# complex, a reactant pattern cut into three pieces, or a molecule joined to
# its pattern only by `.`; and with DeleteMolecules it tested nothing.
#
#   Plus_chain   `A(b!1).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2) -> A(b) + C(b)  DeleteMolecules`
#                on a chain A-B-C: A and C come apart, so it fires at k.
#   Plus_ring    the same rule where A and C are also bonded: the `+` cannot
#                hold, so it never fires.  RuleMonkey fired it.
#   Plus_extra   the same rule on a chain whose B also holds a Y: fires at k,
#                and the Y goes free as a third species, which the keyword
#                allows.
#   Dot_ring     `E(f!1).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2) -> E(f).G(f)  DeleteMolecules` on
#                a ring E-F-G-E: E and G stay bonded, so it fires at k.
#   Dot_chain    the same rule on a chain: the `.` cannot hold, so it never
#                fires.  RuleMonkey fired it.
#   Count_chain  `Xk(c!1).Ck(x!1,y!2).Yk(c!2) -> Xk(c) + Yk(c)`, no keyword,
#                on a chain Xk-Ck-Yk: fires at k (control).
#   Count_ring   the same rule where Xk and Yk are also bonded and the Ck
#                also holds an Ek.  Deleting the Ck leaves two species, the
#                Xk.Yk ring and the Ek, as many as the rule has product
#                patterns.  But Xk and Yk stay joined across the `+`, and the
#                Ek is a species the rule does not write, so it never fires.
#                RuleMonkey, which counted species, fired it.
#   Three_chain  `Ta(b!1,c!2).Tb(a!1).Tc(a!2) -> Ta(b,c) + Tb(a) + Tc(a)` on
#                a chain Tb-Ta-Tc: fires at k.
#   Three_ring   the same rule where Tb and Tc are also bonded: they stay
#                joined across a `+`, so it never fires.  RuleMonkey fired it,
#                the two ends of each deleted bond coming apart.
#   Pair_ring    `Ua(b!1,c!2).Ub(a!1).Uc(a!2) -> Ua(b,c) + Ub(a).Uc(a)` where
#                Ub and Uc are also bonded: the `.` holds, so it fires at k.
#   Pair_chain   the same rule on a chain Ub-Ua-Uc: Ub and Uc come apart, so
#                it never fires.  RuleMonkey fired it.
#   Dotted_onX   `Pj(x!1).Xj(p!1).Qj(t~0) -> Pj(x) + Xj(p).Qj(t~1)`, the Qj
#                joined to the pattern only by `.`, on a chain Pj-Xj-Qj: the
#                Qj leaves with the Xj, so it fires at k.
#   Dotted_onP   the same rule where the Qj hangs off the Pj: it would leave
#                with the Pj, across the `+` and away from the Xj, so it never
#                fires.  RuleMonkey fired it.
#   Dotted_held  `Hp(x!1,y!2).Hx(p!1,q!2).Hq(t~0) -> Hp(x,y!2).Hx(p,q!2) +
#                Hq(t~1)` deletes one of two Hp-Hx bonds, which leaves them
#                joined, and the Hq, joined to the pattern only by `.`, hangs
#                off the Hp: nothing parts it from them, so it never fires.
#                RuleMonkey fired it.
#
# Every rule is unimolecular, so each column follows N*exp(-k*t) or stays N.
begin model
begin parameters
  N     1000
  k     1.0e-3
end parameters
begin molecule types
  A(b,x)
  B(a,c,y)
  C(b,x)
  Y(b)
  E(f,x)
  F(e,g)
  G(f,x)
  Xk(c,y)
  Ck(x,y,e)
  Yk(c,x)
  Ek(c)
  Ta(b,c)
  Tb(a,x)
  Tc(a,x)
  Ua(b,c)
  Ub(a,x)
  Uc(a,x)
  Pj(x,q)
  Xj(p,q)
  Qj(z,t~0~1)
  Hp(x,y,z)
  Hx(p,q)
  Hq(w,t~0~1)
end molecule types
begin seed species
  A(b!1,x).B(a!1,c!2,y).C(b!2,x)               N
  A(b!1,x!3).B(a!1,c!2,y).C(b!2,x!3)           N
  A(b!1,x).B(a!1,c!2,y!4).C(b!2,x).Y(b!4)      N
  E(f!1,x!3).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x!3)             N
  E(f!1,x).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x)                 N
  Xk(c!1,y).Ck(x!1,y!2,e).Yk(c!2,x)            N
  Xk(c!1,y!3).Ck(x!1,y!2,e!4).Yk(c!2,x!3).Ek(c!4)  N
  Ta(b!1,c!2).Tb(a!1,x).Tc(a!2,x)              N
  Ta(b!1,c!2).Tb(a!1,x!3).Tc(a!2,x!3)          N
  Ua(b!1,c!2).Ub(a!1,x!3).Uc(a!2,x!3)          N
  Ua(b!1,c!2).Ub(a!1,x).Uc(a!2,x)              N
  Pj(x!1,q).Xj(p!1,q!2).Qj(z!2,t~0)            N
  Pj(x!1,q!2).Xj(p!1,q).Qj(z!2,t~0)            N
  Hp(x!1,y!2,z!3).Hx(p!1,q!2).Hq(w!3,t~0)      N
end seed species
begin observables
  Molecules  Plus_chain   A(b!1,x).B(a!1,c!2,y).C(b!2,x)
  Molecules  Plus_ring    A(b!1,x!3).B(a!1,c!2,y).C(b!2,x!3)
  Molecules  Plus_extra   A(b!1,x).B(a!1,c!2,y!4).C(b!2,x).Y(b!4)
  Molecules  Dot_ring     E(f!1,x!3).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x!3)
  Molecules  Dot_chain    E(f!1,x).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2,x)
  Molecules  Count_chain  Xk(c!1,y).Ck(x!1,y!2,e).Yk(c!2,x)
  Molecules  Count_ring   Xk(c!1,y!3).Ck(x!1,y!2,e!4).Yk(c!2,x!3).Ek(c!4)
  Molecules  Three_chain  Ta(b!1,c!2).Tb(a!1,x).Tc(a!2,x)
  Molecules  Three_ring   Ta(b!1,c!2).Tb(a!1,x!3).Tc(a!2,x!3)
  Molecules  Pair_ring    Ua(b!1,c!2).Ub(a!1,x!3).Uc(a!2,x!3)
  Molecules  Pair_chain   Ua(b!1,c!2).Ub(a!1,x).Uc(a!2,x)
  Molecules  Dotted_onX   Pj(x!1,q).Xj(p!1,q!2).Qj(z!2,t~0)
  Molecules  Dotted_onP   Pj(x!1,q!2).Xj(p!1,q).Qj(z!2,t~0)
  Molecules  Dotted_held  Hp(x!1,y!2,z!3).Hx(p!1,q!2).Hq(w!3,t~0)
end observables
begin reaction rules
  CutPlus: A(b!1).B(a!1,c!2).C(b!2) -> A(b) + C(b)   k  DeleteMolecules
  CutDot:  E(f!1).F(e!1,g!2).G(f!2) -> E(f).G(f)     k  DeleteMolecules
  Count:   Xk(c!1).Ck(x!1,y!2).Yk(c!2) -> Xk(c) + Yk(c)   k
  Three:   Ta(b!1,c!2).Tb(a!1).Tc(a!2) -> Ta(b,c) + Tb(a) + Tc(a)   k
  Pair:    Ua(b!1,c!2).Ub(a!1).Uc(a!2) -> Ua(b,c) + Ub(a).Uc(a)    k
  Dotted:  Pj(x!1).Xj(p!1).Qj(t~0) -> Pj(x) + Xj(p).Qj(t~1)        k
  Held:    Hp(x!1,y!2).Hx(p!1,q!2).Hq(t~0) -> Hp(x,y!2).Hx(p,q!2) + Hq(t~1)   k
end reaction rules
end model
begin actions
  writeXML({overwrite=>1})
end actions
